&lt;table style=&quot;width: 100%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td style=&quot;border-bottom: 1px solid #AAA; border-right: 1px solid #AAA; text-align: center; width: 25%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:90%;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Assigned Site&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style=&quot;border-bottom: 1px solid #AAA; border-right: 1px solid #AAA; text-align: center; width: 25%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:90%;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Site Director&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style=&quot;border-bottom: 1px solid #AAA; border-right: 1px solid #AAA; text-align: center; width: 25%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:90%;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Research Head&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style=&quot;border-bottom: 1px solid #AAA; text-align: center; width: 25%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:90%;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Assigned MTF&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td style=&quot;border-right: 1px solid #AAA; text-align: center; width: 25%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:80%;&quot;&gt;BioCon Site-11A&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style=&quot;border-right: 1px solid #AAA; text-align: center; width: 25%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:80%;&quot;&gt;Dr. Jonathan Godrich&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:60%;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Department of Psychology&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style=&quot;border-right: 1px solid #AAA; text-align: center; width: 25%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:80%;&quot;&gt;Dr. Jeong Sol-ji&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:60%;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Department of Psychology&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style=&quot;text-align: center; width: 25%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:80%;&quot;&gt;MTF Sigma-313&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:60%;&quot;&gt;(“The Ant Millers”)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Containment Procedures:&lt;/strong&gt; Instances of SCP-5773-1 are to be contained at Biological Containment Site-11A. Site-11A&#039;s atmosphere is to be routinely sterilized once per thirty minute cycle. Foundation personnel assigned to Site-11A are to wear Class-V extreme biological hazard suits at all times.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Interaction with instances of SCP-5773-1 is strictly prohibited for personnel above D-Class. Expired instances of SCP-5773-1 must be disposed of by incineration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5773 is a spontaneous, cognitohazardous phenomenon that affects &lt;em&gt;Homo sapiens&lt;/em&gt;, resulting in subjects&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-568855-1&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; compulsively following one another in a continuous circle. SCP-5773 is caused by the anomalous production of the trail pheromone, Y-802, which is not naturally produced by humans.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP-5773 events typically include between two and twenty individuals. However, due to the inherently social nature of humans, it is speculated that unmitigated SCP-5773 events could involve millions of SCP-5773-1 instances.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is possible to influence SCP-5773 events by impeding the movement of the lead instance of SCP-5773-1. Implementation of this strategy has not only reduced the size of SCP-5773 events but has also allowed for the containment of affected instances.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Instances of SCP-5773-1 display no evidence of self-preservation instincts and will inevitably expire from exhaustion&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-568855-2&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;. As of 21/10/2020, only one instance, identified as SCP-5773-1-A251, has remained conscious during an SCP-5773 event. On 03/03/2017, successful attempts were made by the Foundation to establish communication with the affected instance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Addendum 5773.1&lt;/strong&gt;: Interview Log&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;blockquote&quot; style=&quot;border-radius: 10px; margin: 10px&quot;&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Date&lt;/strong&gt;: March 3rd, 2017&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Interviewer&lt;/strong&gt;: Dr. Jeong Sol-ji, Research Head, &lt;em&gt;Department of Psychology&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Interviewee&lt;/strong&gt;: SCP-5773-1-A251&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-568855-3&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Foreword&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;em&gt;The following interview took place after Foundation staff identified SCP-5773-1-A251 as displaying signs of consciousness and lucidity. Attempts at communication were made throughout the interview&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[Begin Log]&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Sol-ji:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;SCP-5773-1-A251, can you hear me?&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;All instances continue to rotate around in a circle within the containment chamber. Each instances&#039; vision is fixated directly ahead of them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Sol-ji:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Stephen Holme, can you hear me?&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SCP-5773-1-A251&#039;s pupils dilate in response.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Sol-ji:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Stephen, if you can hear me, please blink.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SCP-5773-1-A251 blinks once.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Sol-ji:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Stephen, I&#039;m going to ask you a series of questions. Blink once for yes. Blink twice for no. Is that okay?&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SCP-5773-1-A251 blinks once.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Sol-ji:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Wonderful. Do you understand where you are?&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SCP-5773-1-A251 blinks once.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Sol-ji:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Do you understand what you&#039;re doing?&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SCP-5773-1-A251 blinks once. Shortly after, it blinks twice more.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Sol-ji:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;I&#039;ll repeat the question, Stephen. Do you understand what you&#039;re doing? Are you aware of your actions?&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SCP-5773-1-A251 begins blinking erratically and starts to visibly sweat.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Sol-ji:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Stephen, please, I need you to focus. Do you understand your actions?&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SCP-5773-1-A251&#039;s jaw and neck muscles spasm uncontrollably.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Sol-ji:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Stephen, please, if you could calm down.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SCP-5773-1-A251 turns towards the intercom with a panicked expression and stammers inaudibly.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Sol-ji:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Stephen, please speak up. The microphone didn&#039;t catch that. Do you understand what you&#039;re doing?&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5773-1-A251:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Do any of us?&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[End Log]&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Closing statement:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;SCP-5773-1-A251 failed to respond to any further attempts at questioning and resumed typical SCP-5773-1 behaviour. The subject expired two hours after the interview&#039;s conclusion.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnotes-footer&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Footnotes&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-568855-1&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;1&lt;/a&gt;. Elsewhere designated SCP-5773-1.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-568855-2&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;2&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;quot;Attempts to hydrate and feed instances of SCP-5773-1 through remote feeding tubes to extend their life has been deemed inhumane by the Ethics Committee.&amp;quot; - Dr. J Sol-ji, (January 5th, 2005)&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-568855-3&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;3&lt;/a&gt;. Formerly identified as Stephen Holme, aged 38, a Communications Content Manager at &lt;em&gt;Driver and Vehicle Licensing Agency Swansea&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
